/-
  `O`-version of the §12-type totally separated design, q = 19, rational twist `t` (all three embeddings equal `t`),
  the 27 rows of degrees 4..12.  `O = Z[θ]`, θ³ + θ² − 6θ − 7 = 0.

  Certificates beyond the earlier line: for t = 44/5, 887/100, 8871/1000 (all above t₀ ≈ 8.7951, where the earlier
  one-term-domination line stops) an `S₃`-symmetric test polynomial `q ∈ T_t` with `q(0) = 0` on a different face
  (c211 > 0, c210 < 0, c221 < 0; written in each namespace as orbit coefficients over
  m0, m100, m110, m111, m200, m210, m211, m220, m221, m222).
  In each namespace (`DesignT44over5Cert`, `DesignT887over100Cert`, `DesignT8871over1000Cert`):
    * `q_mem`, `p0_mem`: `q, p0 ∈ T_t` (explicit `Σ_j g(u_j)·h_j`, `g(x) = (x − t)² + 19`), `q_zero`, `p0_zero`.
    * `dq_neg_shift` = Lemma O2 at radius R (R = 100 for t = 44/5, R = 120 for the other two): after `a₁ = d + R`,
      `−Δq` is an explicit sum of two-term AM–GM squares `c·M·(r·u − v)²` plus a polynomial with nonnegative
      coefficients (`ring` + `positivity`).  `dq_neg_of_some_coord_ge` (six coordinates > 0, one of them ≥ R): `Δq < 0`.
      No norm condition is used.
    * `no_design_of_box_table` (ASSUMPTION `hbox`: every piece with all six coordinates ≤ R has `Δq < 0`; positive
      coordinates, nonnegative weights, the design equations for `q` and `p0`): `False`.
      The table `hbox` was checked exactly outside Lean for the totally positive elements of `O` with all embeddings ≤ R
      (B_100: 52,630 elements, 463,410,139 pairs up to the simultaneous Galois action; B_120: 90,942 elements,
      1,382,050,709 pairs up to the Galois action), integer arithmetic on characteristic polynomials (`__int128`, two
      limbs).  Lean does not see `O`.
  The dictionary "design ⟺ `Σ n Δp = p(0)` for all `p ∈ T_t`" (earlier notes, on paper) is not formalised here.
-/
import Mathlib

set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

namespace DesignT44over5Cert

/-- `g(x) = (x − t)² + 19` (`t = 44/5`); the eight points `(t ± i√19)³` are the common zeros of `g(u₁), g(u₂), g(u₃)`. -/
noncomputable def g (x : ℝ) : ℝ := x^2 - (88/5)*x + (2411/25)

